# pbmfix.exe on tests/data/scenarios/SAVEGAME.PBM, a play-by-mail file as a mail program could
# leave it: CR LF line ends, each one doubled. pbmfix writes a line at each carriage return
# that follows text and drops the rest, so the fixed SAVEGAME.PBM has one CR LF per line. Its
# hash is that of the same 133 lines with LF ends. SAVEGAME.OLD is the file as it was, and
# SAVEGAME.FIX is gone, renamed. Under a script the renames are done in BASIC (scriptshell).
# pbmfix reads no key; END's "Press any key to continue" takes the last one.
#! program pbmfix
#! files scenarios/SAVEGAME.PBM scenarios/SAVEGAME.OLD scenarios/SAVEGAME.FIX

repeat space
